{
  "_note": "new_england = visible from Boston/New England per timeanddate's Boston eclipse listings, cross-checked against NASA path/region data. Lunar eclipses are visible everywhere on Earth's night side; per-event global maps live in NASA's lunar eclipse catalog (see _source). Magnitude figures are Boston-local where stated. vis = generous lat/lon bounding box of the full partial-visibility zone for total solar eclipses (used to hide go-scores where the eclipse isn't visible at all; boxes intentionally generous so a score is never hidden without evidence). 2027-08-02 partial zone per Wikipedia (eastern Maine to South/SE Asia); 2028-07-22 per Wikipedia (SE Asia, Australia, Oceania); 2030-11-25 per Wikipedia + space.com (central/southern Africa, Antarctica, Australia, Indonesia, NZ). ne_note is viewer-agnostic: it describes the eclipse, never the viewer's location. Whether a total solar eclipse is visible from the user's location is computed at render time from the vis bounding box (see eclipseVisibleFrom).",
